package mapdemo

// A map whose VALUE is a FIXED ARRAY (docs/SPEC-TABLES.md §2.8): "A VALUE is
// anything a table field can hold ... `[N]T`". The value is an ordinary field
// of the generated entry, so its storage is that field's own row, `T value[N]`
// (§4.2), and its codec is a fixed array's. What is the map's own is the
// HANDLE: an array is not one element, so every map surface hands back the
// ARRAY, and a field past the map makes a stop visible.

table Cells
{
    rows  map[string(8)][3]int32 // [N]T: a fixed extent, complete by construction
    after int32
}
